# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and uncomment what you need.
# `npm run dev` / `npm start` load it automatically - see README.md.

# --- Plugin development ---------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to set here. `npm run dev`/`npm start` already load plugins straight
# from plugins/required/ and plugins/optional/ in the repo with no build step,
# no signing key, and no catalog - drop a plugin folder in and it just shows
# up in Settings. See README.md "Building and running a plugin".
#
# The two variables below are for a different, less common case: testing the
# *real* signed-artifact pipeline locally (the one a packaged installer uses)
# instead of dev-catalog mode. Generate a build with:
#   npm run build --workspace=plugin-sdk
#   npm run plugins:build -- stable development
# then uncomment these, pointing at your own machine's platform subdirectory
# (win32-x64 on Windows, darwin-arm64 on Apple Silicon Mac - each platform
# gets its own catalog, see scripts/build-plugin-repository.mjs) - paths are
# relative to the repo root, regardless of npm's own working directory - and
# restart the server:
# MEMORYLANE_BUNDLED_PLUGIN_REPOSITORY=dist/plugin-repository/v1/stable/win32-x64
# MEMORYLANE_PLUGIN_PUBLIC_KEY=dist/plugin-repository/v1/stable/win32-x64/development-public-key.pem

# --- Everyday dev conveniences ---------------------------------------------
# Point the database/thumbnail cache/logs at a throwaway directory instead of
# your real library, e.g. for testing:
# MEMORYLANE_DATA_DIR=.data/dev

# Skip auto-opening a browser tab on server start:
# MEMORYLANE_NO_OPEN=1

# See README.md "Configuration" for the full list of environment variables.
